<title>UK: Grand Met in sale talks with Sara Lee.</title>
<headline>Grand Met in sale talks with Sara Lee.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British food and drinks group Grand Metropolitan Plc said on Friday it was in the final stages of talks with U.S. group Sara Lee Corporation to sell Grand Met's Brossard cakes business in France and its Fida bakery business in Italy.</p>
<p>Grand Met said an agreement on terms and conditions was expected to be finalised with Sara Lee's subsidiary Sara Lee/DE in the next few weeks.  </p>
<p>Grand Met said Brossard manufactures and markets fresh and frozen cakes and pastries to the French retail market under the brand names Brossard, Gringoire, Savane and Lenotre.</p>
<p>Fida, Brossard's business in Italy, makes and sells fresh cakes to retailers and manufactures under co-packing agreements.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
